1
00:00:00,441 --> 00:00:03,653
Imagine running a small business where invoices arrive every

2
00:00:03,668 --> 00:00:06,218
day. Some are PDFs,

3
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:07,334
some are images,

4
00:00:07,368 --> 00:00:09,356
and the details are never quite in the same

5
00:00:09,371 --> 00:00:12,206
place. You open each file,

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,655
copy the vendor and total into a spreadsheet,

7
00:00:14,677 --> 00:00:16,377
and hope nothing slips through.

8
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,502
One wrong amount throws off the numbers.

9
00:00:20,212 --> 00:00:23,087
One duplicate counts the same expense twice.

10
00:00:23,797 --> 00:00:28,661
That's the workflow I wanted to simplify. Meet InvoiceIQ.

11
00:00:30,441 --> 00:00:34,068
InvoiceIQ turns a document into an editable draft.

12
00:00:34,779 --> 00:00:38,214
It reads PDF text or uses local OCR.

13
00:00:38,937 --> 00:00:41,454
You verify the details before saving.

14
00:00:43,436 --> 00:00:45,019
Here’s the live dashboard.

15
00:00:45,683 --> 00:00:48,921
A fresh browser session starts with an empty workspace.

16
00:00:50,426 --> 00:00:52,918
I choose the fictional Juniper Studio invoice.

17
00:00:53,501 --> 00:00:55,426
InvoiceIQ extracts the vendor,

18
00:00:55,441 --> 00:00:56,800
invoice number, dates,

19
00:00:56,815 --> 00:00:59,001
subtotal, tax, and grand total.

20
00:01:00,426 --> 00:01:01,461
I check the source,

21
00:01:01,476 --> 00:01:02,272
try an edit,

22
00:01:02,287 --> 00:01:04,449
then restore the correct total before saving.

23
00:01:05,026 --> 00:01:07,004
Every extracted field is editable.

24
00:01:08,438 --> 00:01:11,096
The reviewed record is saved in PostgreSQL.

25
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:15,348
I can find it by searching for JS-1042 and

26
00:01:15,363 --> 00:01:16,888
open the saved invoice.

27
00:01:18,424 --> 00:01:20,421
Analytics shows the US dollar total,

28
00:01:20,436 --> 00:01:22,554
recorded tax, and vendor breakdown.

29
00:01:23,119 --> 00:01:25,003
Each currency is tracked separately.

30
00:01:26,441 --> 00:01:28,205
I submit the sample again.

31
00:01:28,917 --> 00:01:32,180
InvoiceIQ warns me before saving because the vendor and

32
00:01:32,195 --> 00:01:33,678
invoice number match.

33
00:01:35,436 --> 00:01:39,407
InvoiceIQ reduces retyping and makes verified records easier to

34
00:01:39,422 --> 00:01:42,890
find. Accuracy still varies by layout,

35
00:01:42,998 --> 00:01:44,883
and line items are future work.

36
00:01:45,546 --> 00:01:48,084
The hosted demo uses a fictional sample.

37
00:01:48,747 --> 00:01:51,369
Local mode also supports scanned documents,

38
00:01:51,513 --> 00:01:53,906
and free hosting may take a moment to wake.

39
00:01:55,441 --> 00:01:58,852
InvoiceIQ. Week one complete.
